        What is in here, and why it is separate
        =======================================

        Everything in this repository that faces Linux, gathered in one place
        so the licence boundary is a directory rather than a judgement call
        made file by file.

        The rest of the tree is Apache-2.0. Linux is GPL-2.0. Nothing here
        changes either of those; this directory only makes the edge visible.


        profile/

        Kernel configuration, composed in order by kit/config, last request
        winning. These are lists of CONFIG_ names and the values we want them
        to have -- our choices about what to build, expressed in the kernel's
        vocabulary. They contain no kernel code.

        profile/modern is the one that removes what a kernel carries for
        machines nobody here will boot. It is written to be read: every entry
        says what it removes and, where it was found by measuring, what the
        measurement was.


        replace/

        Assembly that stands in for a file the kernel already builds, put in
        its place by kit/asm_replace before the kernel is configured. This is
        the part that is genuinely entangled: a replacement occupies the same
        position in the build as the GPL-2.0 file it displaces, and whether a
        given one is an independent implementation or a derivative work is a
        question about that file and not about this directory.

        Nothing here declares a licence for those files. That is the owner's
        to decide, per file, and this note exists so the decision is not made
        by accident.


        What is not in here, and cannot be

        The module itself -- src/Makefile, src/Kconfig, src/core.c and the
        library they build -- stays where it is. kbuild requires a module's
        Makefile and Kconfig to sit at the root of the directory it compiles,
        and build.sh symlinks that root to src/. Moving them here would mean
        moving the whole library with them.

        The claim and displace tables are still inside build.sh, around the
        KERNEL CONFIG label. They are the other place this repository writes
        into the kernel tree: a claim adds a __HAVE_ARCH_ line and a
        declaration to the architecture's string header, and a displace
        comments an object out of an architecture's lib/Makefile. Both edit
        files under linux/, which is downloaded and not part of this
        repository, and both are undone by a fresh extraction.
